+---
+description: Specstory is local-only; never stage, commit, push, or review it
+alwaysApply: true
+---
+
+# Specstory: local / generated only
+
+Specstory output is **local developer metadata**, not project source. Treat it like editor cache.
+
+## Do not track or ship
+
+- Do **not** commit, push, or include Specstory files or folders in PRs or code reviews.
+- Do **not** suggest adding Specstory paths to shared docs unless explaining how to ignore them.
+
+## Git
+
+- Ensure `.gitignore` includes Specstory patterns (add or extend if new variants appear):
+
+```gitignore
+# Specstory (local/generated; never commit)
+specstory/
+*.specstory
+.specstory/
+```
+
+## Before every commit
+
+1. Run `git status` and scan for any path containing `specstory` or `.specstory`.
+2. If any appear **staged**, unstage them (`git restore --staged â€¦` on those paths) and confirm `.gitignore` covers them.
+3. Do not use `--no-verify` or other flags to bypass checks in order to commit Specstory artifacts.
+
+## If Specstory was committed by mistake
+
+Remove from tracking while keeping local files: `git rm -r --cached <paths>` then commit the ignore fix separatelyâ€”only when the user asks for a commit.
