+# Conviva Analytics â€” Restoration Guide
+
+Conviva is **temporarily disabled**, not removed. Implementation code is preserved in comments and no-op stubs so the player keeps working without the Conviva SDK.
+
+**Master switch (JavaScript):** `src/convivaConfig.ts` â†’ `CONVIVA_DISABLED = true`
+
+Search the repo for `CONVIVA_DISABLED` to find every touchpoint.
+
+---
+
+## Quick checklist
+
+| Step | Action |
+|------|--------|
+| 1 | Re-add native dependencies (Gradle + CocoaPods) |
+| 2 | Restore native implementations (uncomment originals, remove stubs) |
+| 3 | Re-register native modules |
+| 4 | Set `CONVIVA_DISABLED = false` in `src/convivaConfig.ts` |
+| 5 | Restore TypeScript (`src/ConvivaHelper.ts`, `src/Video.tsx`) and uncomment `export {ConvivaHelper} from './ConvivaHelper'` in `src/index.ts` (`CONVIVA_EXPORT_HIDDEN_FROM_PUBLIC_API`) |
+| 6 | Restore `RCTVideo.swift` (uncomment `CONVIVA_DISABLED: original` blocks) + `RCTVideoManager.swift` |
+| 7 | Uncomment Android `@ReactProp` / `@ReactMethod` bodies |
+| 8 | Run `yarn build` and rebuild the consumer app (Android + iOS) |
+
+---
+
+## 1. Re-add dependencies
+
+### Android â€” `android/build.gradle`
+
+Uncomment:
+
+```gradle
+implementation 'com.conviva.sdk:conviva-core-sdk:4.0.50'
+implementation 'com.conviva.sdk:conviva-media3-sdk:4.0.1'
+```
+
+Then sync Gradle in the consumer app.
+
+**Docs:** [Android quick integration](https://pulse.conviva.com/learning-center/content/sensor_developer_center/sensor_integration/android/android_quick_integration.htm)
+
+### iOS â€” `react-native-video.podspec`
+
+Uncomment (iOS + tvOS):
+
+```ruby
+ss.ios.dependency 'ConvivaSDK','4.3.0'
+ss.ios.dependency 'ConvivaAVFoundation', '4.3.0'
+ss.tvos.dependency 'ConvivaSDK','4.3.0'
+ss.tvos.dependency 'ConvivaAVFoundation', '4.3.0'
+```
+
+> **Note:** The podspec may also list alternate pinned versions in comments (e.g. `4.0.52` / `4.0.58`). Use the versions your Conviva account and release process require.
+
+In the **consumer app** (not only this package):
+
+```bash
+cd <your-app-ios-folder>
+pod install
+```
+
+**Docs:** [iOS stream sensor](https://pulse.conviva.com/learning-center/content/sensor_developer_center/sensor_integration/ios/ios_stream_sensor.html)
+
+---
+
+## 2. Restore native implementations
+
+### Android â€” `android/src/main/java/com/brentvatne/react/ConvivaHelper.kt`
+
+1. Re-add `com.conviva.sdk` dependencies in `android/build.gradle` (step 1 above).
+2. Replace the stub with the archived original (same directory, **not** compiled while disabled):
+
+```bash
+cp android/src/main/java/com/brentvatne/react/ConvivaHelper.kt.original \
+   android/src/main/java/com/brentvatne/react/ConvivaHelper.kt
+```
+
+3. Ensure real SDK imports are active (`com.conviva.sdk.*`) â€” the archive already uses them.
+
+### Android â€” `android/src/main/java/com/brentvatne/react/ReactVideoPackage.kt`
+
+Uncomment module registration:
+
+```kotlin
+ConvivaHelper(reactContext),
+```
+
+### Android â€” `android/src/main/java/com/brentvatne/exoplayer/ReactExoplayerView.java`
+
+Restore SDK imports and remove stub imports:
+
+```java
+// Restore:
+import com.conviva.sdk.ConvivaVideoAnalytics;
+import com.conviva.sdk.ConvivaSdkConstants;
+
+// Remove (added for CONVIVA_DISABLED):
+import com.brentvatne.react.ConvivaVideoAnalytics;
+import com.brentvatne.react.ConvivaSdkConstants;
+```
+
+Search for `CONVIVA_DISABLED` in this file for any other commented import lines.
+
+### iOS â€” `ios/Video/RCTConvivaHelper.swift`
+
+1. Uncomment `import ConvivaSDK` at the top.
+2. Delete the **no-op stub** `class RCTConvivaHelper` (the short class with empty method bodies).
+3. Uncomment the block marked **`CONVIVA_DISABLED: ORIGINAL IMPLEMENTATION`** at the bottom.
+
+> **Google IMA (`GoogleInteractiveMediaAds`):** Do **not** add `import GoogleInteractiveMediaAds` to this file while restoring Conviva. The Conviva helper and its preserved original implementation only reference IMA as metadata strings (e.g. `"Google IMA SDK"`); they do not use IMA SDK types. Unconditional IMA imports here break consumer apps that do not set `$RNVideoUseGoogleIMA=true` in the Podfile. Keep IMA optional in `RCTVideo.swift` and `ios/Video/Features/RCTIMAAdsManager.swift` (`#if USE_GOOGLE_IMA`).
+
+### Android â€” IMA stubs (`useExoplayerIMA=false`, default)
+
+When ads are **disabled** (`useExoplayerIMA = false` in the consumer `android/build.gradle`), the library ships no-op stubs under:
+
+- `android/src/main/java/com/google/ads/interactivemedia/v3/api/` (and `v3/impl/zze.java`)
+- `android/src/main/java/androidx/media3/exoplayer/ima/ImaAdsLoader.java`
+
+`ReactExoplayerView.java` must compile against these stubs (no Play Services / real IMA JAR). When you enable ads, set `useExoplayerIMA = true`; Gradle excludes the stub packages and pulls `androidx.media3:media3-exoplayer-ima` instead.
+
+### iOS â€” `ios/Video/RCTConvivaHelper.m`
+
+Uncomment the `@interface RCT_EXTERN_MODULE(ConvivaHelper, RCTViewManager) ... @end` block between the `START original implementation` / `END` markers so the Conviva native module is registered on the bridge again.
+
+### iOS â€” `ios/Video/RCTVideo.swift`
+
+Conviva logic is disabled in two places: the **Conviva methods block** (no-op stubs + preserved originals) and a few **scattered call sites** elsewhere in the file.
+
+#### A. Conviva methods block (~lines 2558â€“2860)
+
+Search for:
+
+```
+// ----- START CONVIVA_DISABLED no-op stubs
+```
+
+For **each** method between START and END:
+
+1. Delete the active no-op stub (e.g. `func initConvivaManually() { /* CONVIVA_DISABLED: no-op */ }`).
+2. Uncomment the matching `/* CONVIVA_DISABLED: original â€¦ */` block directly below it.
+3. Remove duplicate `@objc` if your editor leaves two declarationsâ€”only one live method should remain.
+
+Methods restored this way:
+
+| Method | Notes |
+|--------|--------|
+| `setConvivaContentInfo` | Already stores `_convivaContentInfo`; no change needed unless you replaced it |
+| `initConvivaManually` | |
+| `setConvivaPlayerReferenceManually` | |
+| `destroyConvivaManually` | |
+| `reportPlaybackEventWaitEnded` | |
+| `initConvivaSession` | |
+| `initConvivaAnalyticsSession` | |
+| `setPlayerRef` | |
+| `destroyConvivaAnalyticsSession` | |
+| `reportAdPlaying` / `reportAdPaused` / `reportAdBuffering` / `reportAdBitrate` | Require `import ConvivaSDK` |
+
+Also in this block:
+
+- **`setPlayerPreFetchEnable`:** delete the active one-line assign; uncomment the `/* CONVIVA_DISABLED: original` block with the `getVideoAnalyticsInstance()` guard.
+- **`setAdsEnabled`:** uncomment the `reportPlaybackEventWaitStarted` `if` block inside `#if USE_GOOGLE_IMA`.
+
+#### B. Scattered call sites (search `CONVIVA_DISABLED` in this file)
+
+Uncomment these after restoring `RCTConvivaHelper.swift`:
+
+| Location | What to restore |
+|----------|-----------------|
+| Player creation (`_player = AVPlayer()`) | `initConvivaSession()` |
+| `setSeek` | `reportSeekStarted` / `reportSeekEnded` blocks |
+| `removeFromSuperview` / teardown | `destroyConvivaAnalyticsSession()` `if` block |
+| `handleReadyForDisplay` | `reportPlaybackEventWaitStarted` `if` block (IMA) |
+| `handlePlayerItemStatusChange` | `RCTConvivaHelper.isPlayerRefSet = false` block |
+
+#### C. Top of file
+
+Uncomment:
+
+```swift
+import ConvivaSDK
+```
+
+Restore **`RCTConvivaHelper.swift`** (real implementation) **before** or **together with** step A so uncommented bodies compile.
+
+### iOS â€” `ios/Video/RCTVideoManager.swift`
+
+Uncomment the bodies of:
+
+- `initConvivaManually(_:)`
+- `setConvivaPlayerReferenceManually(_:)`
+- `destroyConvivaManually(_:)`
+- `reportPlaybackEventWaitEnded(_:)`
+
+Remove the `// CONVIVA_DISABLED: no-op` lines above each commented block.
+
+### iOS â€” `ios/Video/RCTVideoManager.m`
+
+Conviva view properties and `RCT_EXTERN_METHOD` declarations were **left exported** on purpose. No change is usually required here unless you previously commented exports out in a local branchâ€”if so, restore any commented `RCT_EXPORT_VIEW_PROPERTY` / `RCT_EXTERN_METHOD` lines for Conviva.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Restore Android bridge wiring
+
+### `android/src/main/java/com/brentvatne/exoplayer/ReactExoplayerViewManager.kt`
+
+Uncomment the bodies of:
+
+- `setConvivaVideoAnalyticsState`
+- `setConvivaContentInfo`
+- `setDestroyConvivaAfterReload`
+
+### `android/src/main/java/com/brentvatne/react/VideoManagerModule.kt`
+
+Uncomment the bodies of:
+
+- `initConvivaManually`
+- `setConvivaPlayerReferenceManually`
+- `reportPlaybackEventWaitEnded`
+- `destroyConvivaManually`
+
+---
+
+## 4. Restore JavaScript / TypeScript
+
+### `src/convivaConfig.ts`
+
+```ts
+export const CONVIVA_DISABLED = false;
+```
+
+### `src/index.ts`
+
+Uncomment the `ConvivaHelper` re-export (search `CONVIVA_EXPORT_HIDDEN_FROM_PUBLIC_API`):
+
+```ts
+export {ConvivaHelper} from './ConvivaHelper';
+```
+
+### `src/ConvivaHelper.ts`
+
+1. Uncomment `import NativeConvivaHelper from './specs/NativeConvivaHelper';`
+2. Remove the no-op `ConvivaHelper` object (methods that check `CONVIVA_DISABLED`).
+3. Uncomment the **`CONVIVA_DISABLED: original implementation`** block at the bottom (or replace the file body with that block).
+
+### `src/Video.tsx`
+
+`useImperativeHandle` only exposes Conviva ref methods when `CONVIVA_DISABLED` is `false`.
+
+For each Conviva ref method, remove the `Promise.resolve()` no-op and uncomment the `NativeVideoManager.*` call:
+
+- `initConvivaManually`
+- `destroyConvivaManually`
+- `setConvivaPlayerReferenceManually`
+- `reportPlaybackEventWaitEnded`
+
+### Rebuild published JS
+
+From the package root:
+
+```bash
+yarn build
+```
+
+This refreshes `lib/` (`ConvivaHelper.js`, `convivaConfig.js`, `Video.js`, etc.).
+
+---
+
+## 5. Verify after restore
+
+1. **TypeScript:** `yarn tsc --noEmit`
+2. **Lint (optional):** `yarn eslint src/ConvivaHelper.ts src/convivaConfig.ts src/Video.tsx`
+3. **Android:** clean build; confirm no unresolved `com.conviva.sdk` symbols.
+4. **iOS:** `pod install` + Xcode build; confirm `ConvivaSDK` / `ConvivaAVFoundation` resolve.
+5. **Runtime:** play VOD/live content with ads; confirm Conviva sessions and ad metrics in the Conviva Pulse dashboard (use Touchstone if applicable).
+
+---
+
+## What stays disabled today (reference)
+
+| Layer | Mechanism |
+|-------|-----------|
+| JS | `CONVIVA_DISABLED` + no-op `ConvivaHelper` (not re-exported from `src/index.ts`) + Conviva ref methods omitted from `Video` ref while disabled |
+| Android | Conviva Gradle deps commented out; `ConvivaHelper` stub; module unregistered; some `@ReactProp` / `@ReactMethod` bodies commented |
+| iOS | Conviva pods commented out; `RCTConvivaHelper` stub (no `ConvivaSDK` / **no** `GoogleInteractiveMediaAds` import); `.m` module registration commented; `RCTVideo` Conviva methods are no-ops with originals in `/* CONVIVA_DISABLED: original */` blocks; scattered `_RCTConvivaHelper` calls commented; `RCTVideoManager` bridge methods no-op |
+
+**Files with preserved original code (search `CONVIVA_DISABLED` or `ORIGINAL IMPLEMENTATION`):**
+
+- `src/index.ts` (Conviva export commented; search `CONVIVA_EXPORT_HIDDEN_FROM_PUBLIC_API`)
+- `src/convivaConfig.ts`
+- `src/ConvivaHelper.ts`
+- `src/Video.tsx`
+- `android/build.gradle`
+- `android/src/main/java/com/brentvatne/react/ConvivaHelper.kt` (stub while disabled)
+- `android/src/main/java/com/brentvatne/react/ConvivaHelper.kt.original` (full implementation archive)
+- `android/src/main/java/com/brentvatne/react/ReactVideoPackage.kt`
+- `android/src/main/java/com/brentvatne/react/VideoManagerModule.kt`
+- `android/src/main/java/com/brentvatne/exoplayer/ReactExoplayerView.java`
+- `android/src/main/java/com/brentvatne/exoplayer/ReactExoplayerViewManager.kt`
+- `react-native-video.podspec`
+- `ios/Video/RCTConvivaHelper.swift`
+- `ios/Video/RCTConvivaHelper.m`
+- `ios/Video/RCTVideo.swift`
+- `ios/Video/RCTVideoManager.swift`
+- `ios/Video/RCTVideoManager.m`
+
+`ios/Video/Features/RCTIMAAdsManager.swift` was not modified; it still calls `RCTVideo._RCTConvivaHelper`, which routes to the stub until restoration.
+
+---
+
+## Rollback (disable again)
+
+Reverse the checklist: comment dependencies, restore stubs, set `CONVIVA_DISABLED = true`, comment out `export {ConvivaHelper}...` in `src/index.ts`, run `yarn build`. Per-file banners document the exact comment blocks to restore.
+
+When re-applying the stub in `RCTConvivaHelper.swift`, keep only `import AVFoundation` and `import React` (plus commented `// import ConvivaSDK`). Do **not** reintroduce `import GoogleInteractiveMediaAds`.
+
+---
+
+## Troubleshooting (iOS build)
+
+### `No such module 'GoogleInteractiveMediaAds'` without enabling ads
+
+**Cause:** Unconditional `import GoogleInteractiveMediaAds` in `RCTConvivaHelper.swift` while the consumer Podfile does not set `$RNVideoUseGoogleIMA=true` (so the IMA CocoaPod is not installed).
+
+**Fix (library maintainers):** Remove that import from the Conviva stub; IMA remains gated in `RCTVideo.swift` / `RCTIMAAdsManager.swift`.
+
+**Fix (app developers, temporary):** Either enable IMA in the Podfile (`$RNVideoUseGoogleIMA=true` then `pod install`) or upgrade to a library revision that drops the stray import from `RCTConvivaHelper.swift`.
